n the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $68.9m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 56.5% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 23.3% to 20.0% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 20.0%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-3.3% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $1.3m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819974/000181997426000014/0001819974-26-000014-index.htm","accession":"0001819974-26-000014"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 12.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.12,"consecutive":2,"current":0.2,"current_display":"20.0%","threshold_display":"12.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 81.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.81,"consecutive":2,"current":1.621,"current_display":"162.1%","threshold_display":"81.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":0.021,"current_display":"2.1%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.208,"current_display":"0.21","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareh